# Derived by hand from ruling TC (places are counted as they are built) and Semantics ch. 8 ("takes the next number"): the wide arm builds places 1 and 2, so `more` is 3 and the one-place clause of `@Tail` is 4; the narrow arm builds place 1, so `more` is 2 and the two-place clause of `@Tail` is 3 and 4; the last label is 5 in both.
test the_wide_arm

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Label(text="panel")
    1: Ui.Label(text="loud")
    2: Ui.Button(label="wide")
    3: Ui.Button(label="more")
    4: Ui.Label(text="tail")
    5: Ui.Label(text="inner 0 more 0")

tick 1
  in:
    3: click
  changed:
    5: Ui.Label(text="inner 0 more 1")

tick 2
  in:
    2: click
  changed:
    5: Ui.Label(text="inner 1 more 1")

